skill: "renewal-and-liability-watch"
sections[3]:
  - "# renewal-and-liability-watch\n\nWatch the contract register for renewal windows and liability exposure: auto-renewal deadlines with notice cutoffs, liability caps against the policy floor, uncapped exposures and insurance requirements. Use monthly, and whenever a contract is signed, amended or assigned.\n\nOwner: role-contract-manager (pod-gna, legal). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"contract register contracts.toon (parties, term, renewal mechanism, notice window, caps, insurance); liability policy liability-cap-policy.toon; amendments history\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/legal/renewal-calendar.toon with T-120|T-90|T-60 triggers and notice deadlines; liability-register.toon with cap vs floor, uncapped[], insurance status\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load the contract register and reconcile it against the amendment history; a register entry whose latest amendment is not reflected is corrected first, with the source amendment cited.\n2. Extract per contract: term end, renewal mechanism (auto, opt-out, renegotiate), the notice deadline that exits or renegotiates, and who owns that decision.\n3. Build the renewal calendar with T-120, T-90 and T-60 triggers relative to each notice deadline; auto-renewing contracts get their trigger pinned to the notice cutoff, not the term end.\n4. Validate liability caps against liability-cap-policy.toon: cap at or above the floor passes; below the floor is flagged with the amendment path (raise cap, narrow scope, insure).\n5. List uncapped exposures: indemnities without caps, unlimited carve-outs (IP breach, confidentiality, bodily injury where uncapped by law is separate from uncapped by omission); each cites the clause text.\n6. Check insurance requirements per contract: required coverage, evidence on file, expiry against the contract term; missing certificates are tracked as open items with owners.\n7. Compute the aggregate uncapped exposure by counterparty with run_command so concentration is visible, not scattered across files.\n8. Write renewal-calendar.toon and liability-register.toon; emit ask_question for renewal decisions inside the T-60 window and for any uncapped exposure without a recorded acceptance.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nrenewal decisions to owners via ask_question; register updates to contracts.toon.\n"
